{"title":"2020 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_24\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 24</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(using_answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (using answer choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheMathGeek\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheMathGeek</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Robin_“The_Smartest_Dude”_Shang\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Robin “The Smartest Dude” Shang</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_STEMbreezy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by STEMbreezy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_24\">Problem 24</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 24\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A large square region is paved with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> gray square tiles, each measuring <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> inches on a side. A border <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inches wide surrounds each tile. The figure below shows the case for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece448a1996d075309961bd398a7c8afc99a50e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" />, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/8/7080fdbf6e7385fb60b23d885788d3bd7eda12a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$576$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> gray tiles cover <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/c/82c2d0dd5aaa1283b9aed82f11835088b120a596.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of the area of the large square region. What is the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/a/11ad8a0a7d748c67f54b6c7d20551b8a84672174.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> for this larger value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/8/a28578f91569670ce8f5d1c27b4ea637a09a75a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/d/8fd65da31faff2077b0526ddc1de09fec17ff2df.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(13,0)--(13,13)--(0,13)--cycle); filldraw((1,1)--(4,1)--(4,4)--(1,4)--cycle, mediumgray); filldraw((1,5)--(4,5)--(4,8)--(1,8)--cycle, mediumgray); filldraw((1,9)--(4,9)--(4,12)--(1,12)--cycle, mediumgray); filldraw((5,1)--(8,1)--(8,4)--(5,4)--cycle, mediumgray); filldraw((5,5)--(8,5)--(8,8)--(5,8)--cycle, mediumgray); filldraw((5,9)--(8,9)--(8,12)--(5,12)--cycle, mediumgray); filldraw((9,1)--(12,1)--(12,4)--(9,4)--cycle, mediumgray); filldraw((9,5)--(12,5)--(12,8)--(9,8)--cycle, mediumgray); filldraw((12,12)--(12,9)--(9,9)--(9,12)--cycle, mediumgray); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\t\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/a/f1ac2797b0517082c78c46b2b633595ee573261e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{6}{25} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\frac{1}{4} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\frac{9}{25} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\frac{7}{16} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\frac{9}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"408\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of the shaded region is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/f/56f9d6b57a506f30c3d6f2921a4fcab6aa057426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(24s)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"19\" />. To find the area of the large square, we note that there is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-inch border between each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> pairs of consecutive squares, as well as from between the first/last squares and the large square, for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/a/53aff321efa2b1bc70e16b5d32fe12d2ec966157.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23+2 = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" /> times the length of the border, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/2/3e2957656b465d14e9c4a809672fc26bdba6487e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. Adding this to the total length of the consecutive squares, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cbc509b3a4d19d5c99f9c7d47719f516b956023.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24s$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, the side length of the large square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/1/df1cb5b42ae9a5f059aeedc31d93739e076e11f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(24s+25d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />, yielding the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/b/0fb755716c37e8b171b2012a06c9f7f99a94715d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(24s)^2}{(24s+25d)^2}=\\frac{64}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"156\" height=\"43\" />. Taking the square root of both sides (and using the fact that lengths are non-negative) gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2efd8de5d5a26c91d94b4e7c2edd5530bcc399bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{24s}{24s+25d}=\\frac{8}{10} = \\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"162\" height=\"39\" />, and cross-multiplying now gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a81f5b1dd44cbbc83639ae6b0494553f62b561d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120s = 96s + 100d \\Rightarrow 24s = 100d \\Rightarrow \\frac{d}{s} = \\frac{24}{100} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{6}{25}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"452\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nNote: Once we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bff1fcf433848d06773d6132e347fbb2a95837b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{24s}{24s+25d} = \\tfrac{4}{5},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"96\" height=\"24\" /> to ease computation, we may take the reciprocal of both sides to yield <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebcc3bab939369d88270be897c1b6b5efad99b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{24s+25d}{24s} = 1 + \\tfrac{25d}{24s} = \\tfrac{5}{4},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"175\" height=\"24\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/0/780001eb373fa197290204131e57e7063d8000ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{25d}{24s} = \\tfrac{1}{4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"66\" height=\"24\" /> Multiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5a726819455681a448896b15e91be40d8811cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{24}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"15\" height=\"21\" /> yields the same answer as before. \n</p><p>~peace09\n</p><p>~Minor Edits by WrenMath\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>WLOG (Without Loss of Generality), we may let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb16e2177f55574e2538c0d9b240b1ee7d46d767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> will be determined by the scale of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and we are only interested in the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/a/11ad8a0a7d748c67f54b6c7d20551b8a84672174.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />). Then, as the total area of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/8/7080fdbf6e7385fb60b23d885788d3bd7eda12a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$576$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> gray tiles is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/8/7080fdbf6e7385fb60b23d885788d3bd7eda12a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$576$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, the large square has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/2/342cc394f799a3f93c09beda4641bbacc55e52e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{576}{0.64} = 900$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" />, making the side of the large square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/a/7cae0625b7a3e38e07e98de5e91b6994ad009798.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{900}=30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />. As in Solution 1, the side length of the large square consists of the total length of the gray tiles and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> lots of the border, so the length of the border is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52ea5760ffe1cf3d7fd2d90031e59096506c52bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = \\frac{30-24}{25} = \\frac{6}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"141\" height=\"37\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/2/ff22d628baf4818880d2f68fe90f4ccf1fd36912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{s}=d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"47\" height=\"37\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb16e2177f55574e2538c0d9b240b1ee7d46d767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/2/9820ddf783996c6abe4c5ee278a5b1b63744b2f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{6}{25}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"69\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28using_answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(using_answer_choices)\">Solution 3 (using answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (using answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in Solution 2, we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/1/231cd70adaea591bac095e7290c91c1e9d41d8a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> without loss of generality. For sufficiently large <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we can approximate the percentage of the area covered by the gray tiles by subdividing most of the region into congruent squares, as shown:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f45566b58dbf56a06503f7f627b969c1422d7e10.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(13,0)--(13,13)--(0,13)--cycle); filldraw((1,1)--(4,1)--(4,4)--(1,4)--cycle, mediumgray); filldraw((1,5)--(4,5)--(4,8)--(1,8)--cycle, mediumgray); filldraw((1,9)--(4,9)--(4,12)--(1,12)--cycle, mediumgray); filldraw((5,1)--(8,1)--(8,4)--(5,4)--cycle, mediumgray); filldraw((5,5)--(8,5)--(8,8)--(5,8)--cycle, mediumgray); filldraw((5,9)--(8,9)--(8,12)--(5,12)--cycle, mediumgray); filldraw((9,1)--(12,1)--(12,4)--(9,4)--cycle, mediumgray); filldraw((9,5)--(12,5)--(12,8)--(9,8)--cycle, mediumgray); filldraw((9,9)--(12,9)--(12,12)--(9,12)--cycle, mediumgray);  for(int i = 1; i &lt;= 13; i += 4){ draw((1,i)--(13,i), red); draw((i,1)--(i,13), red); } [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\t\nEach red square has side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab43a830baf08af5d019ed75a4bf769365b0986.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />, so by solving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6bee99ca11559593f7604da9427add3bf04bd88a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1^2}{(1+d)^2} = \\frac{64}{100} \\iff \\frac{1}{1+d} = \\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"256\" height=\"43\" />, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a374307f97c5b56e01364c0ed37f37815af35a7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" />. The actual fraction of the total area covered by the gray tiles will be slightly less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/4/6945e7b4fa97e67da4c816b46b5049cf8b8fe15e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{(1+d)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"64\" height=\"41\" />, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/9/4794448f4623e44828988e4ed48b41c8725e6543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{(1+d)^2} &gt; \\frac{64}{100} \\iff \\frac{1}{1+d} &gt; \\frac{4}{5} \\iff d &lt; \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"356\" height=\"42\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/a/11ad8a0a7d748c67f54b6c7d20551b8a84672174.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, since we are assuming <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb16e2177f55574e2538c0d9b240b1ee7d46d767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />) is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, and the only choice that satisfies this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/2/9820ddf783996c6abe4c5ee278a5b1b63744b2f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{6}{25}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"69\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>Note the answer cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> because this is only an approximation. The closest answer choice is  A.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Pack all tiles together to form a square.  As this square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/f/14f3d3d80ca362dad5f043df8b185fddb39a540d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(24s \\times 24s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" /> covers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/c/82c2d0dd5aaa1283b9aed82f11835088b120a596.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of the big square, that means its length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/7/bb7e03ccc8985ba9d029ea4add6e3e15ab9a953a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> long of the big square's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/855662ab92c0c1a4c0d0330cc50eeec3afb776c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(24s+25d \\times 24s+25d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"191\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/6998d0f9a0f99536d6d0fd68c4fb30facf1a0eef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25d : 24s = 2 : 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"129\" height=\"14\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/d/61d138e31d37789c208ad647d1f992c9a20fa6f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{s} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{6}{25}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"109\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/d/eadb11777a0947a651b7989f19eb781af0c06c54.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(10,0)--(10,10)--(0,10)--cycle); filldraw((0,0)--(8,0)--(8,8)--(0,8)--cycle, mediumgray); filldraw((8,8)--(8,10)--(10,10)--(10,8)--cycle, mediumgreen); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheMathGeek\">Video Solution by TheMathGeek</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheMathGeek\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IsqueKZCKbk&amp;t=11s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IsqueKZCKbk&amp;t=11s</a>\n</p><p>~TheMathGeek\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X\">Video Solution by Math-X</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtube/UnVo6jZ3Wnk?si=Qs8zS0YEfg1iP-Y2&amp;t=5584\">https://youtube/UnVo6jZ3Wnk?si=Qs8zS0YEfg1iP-Y2&amp;t=5584</a> \n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vnk73Kd8t4o&amp;list=PL73YVYWi-yG8Exr884k6y3eq8VBFMZRIF&amp;index=24\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vnk73Kd8t4o&amp;list=PL73YVYWi-yG8Exr884k6y3eq8VBFMZRIF&amp;index=24</a>\n</p><p><i>~Education, the Study of Everything </i>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Robin_.E2.80.9CThe_Smartest_Dude.E2.80.9D_Shang\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Robin_“The_Smartest_Dude”_Shang\">Video Solution by Robin “The Smartest Dude” Shang</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Robin “The Smartest Dude” Shang\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/t8MVmKEyUhw\">https://youtu.be/t8MVmKEyUhw</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/UpCURw5Moig?t=31\">https://youtu.be/UpCURw5Moig?t=31</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/NHYB0VI3dcY\">https://youtu.be/NHYB0VI3dcY</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YnwkBZTv5Fw?t=1515\">https://youtu.be/YnwkBZTv5Fw?t=1515</a>\n</p><p>~Interstigation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_STEMbreezy\">Video Solution by STEMbreezy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by STEMbreezy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wq8EUCe5oQU?t=353\">https://youtu.be/wq8EUCe5oQU?t=353</a>\n</p><p>~STEMbreezy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mGQw1yALXYM&amp;t=3904s\">https://youtu.be/mGQw1yALXYM&amp;t=3904s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See al